Description: Provides the functions of the Genetic Algorithm Toolbox for
    'MATLAB' developed at the University of Sheffield (Chipperfield et al.
    1994, <https://github.com/UoS-CODeM/GA-Toolbox>), rewritten in R.
    It includes operators for creating binary, integer and real-valued
    populations, rank-based and linear fitness assignment, roulette wheel
    and stochastic universal sampling selection, single-point, multi-point,
    shuffle and reduced surrogate crossover, discrete, intermediate and line
    recombination, discrete and breeder genetic algorithm mutation,
    reinsertion of offspring, and migration between subpopulations.
